Perfect! Here's a checklist and automation guide to help you enroll existing AVD session hosts into Microsoft Intune, especially if they are Hybrid Azure AD joined.

✅ Checklist for Automating Intune Enrollment (Hybrid Azure AD Joined VMs)
🔹 Prerequisites
	• ✅ Windows 10/11 Enterprise multi-session
	• ✅ Hybrid Azure AD Join configured via Azure AD Connect
	• ✅ Intune license assigned to users
	• ✅ Network access to domain controllers

🛠 Automation via Group Policy (Recommended)
1. Create a Group Policy Object (GPO)
	• Open Group Policy Management Console on your domain controller.
	• Create a new GPO and name it something like Intune Enrollment for AVD.
2. Configure MDM Enrollment Settings
Navigate to:
Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > MDM
Enable:
Enable automatic MDM enrollment using default Azure AD credentials
Set to:
	• User Credential
	• Apply and close.
3. Link GPO to AVD OU
	• Link the GPO to the Organizational Unit (OU) that contains your AVD session hosts.
4. Force Group Policy Update (Optional)
You can run this remotely or via a startup script:

gpupdate /force


🧪 Verification Steps
	• On the AVD session host, go to: Settings > Accounts > Access work or school
	• Confirm that the device is enrolled in Intune.
	• Check the Intune Admin Center under: Devices > Windows > All devices

🧰 Optional: PowerShell Script for Manual Trigger
If you want to trigger enrollment manually or remotely:

$EnrollmentTrigger = New-Object -ComObject Schedule.Service
$EnrollmentTrigger.Connect()
$TaskFolder = $EnrollmentTrigger.GetFolder("\Microsoft\Windows\EnterpriseMgmt")
$TaskFolder.GetTasks(0) | ForEach-Object { $_.Run("") }


❌ Azure AD Joined VMs
For Azure AD joined VMs, you must redeploy with the “Enroll in Intune” option enabled in the Azure portal. There is no supported method to enroll them post-deployment.

